    "evidence_text": "Therefore, the model trained with the proposed training framework reduces relative 14\\% character error rate, compared to original model which has the similar real-time capability.\n\nEMA method is utilized with model averaging and BMUF to further decrease the character error rate (CER).\n\nWe choose state-level minimum bayes risk (sMBR)  among a number of sequence discriminative criterion is proposed, such as maximum mutual information (MMI)  and minimum phone error (MPE)  .\n\nMPE and sMBR are designed to minimize the expected error of different granularity of labels, while CE aims to minimizes expected frame error, and MMI aims to minimizes expected sentence error.\n\nHowever, it also leads to much more computation and higher RTF, so that the recognition result can not be displayed in real time.\n\nThe performance metric of the system in Mandarin is reported with character error rate (CER).\n\nThe teacher model is trained with CE.\n\nlayers decreases absolute 0.73% approximately compared with CE models, so the improvement of sequence discriminative learning is promising.\n\nAs a result, with the Shenma model, only about 14% data usage achieves lower CER, and it leads to great time and cost saving with less labeled data.",
